<h2>1. Identity and Contact Details of the Controller</h2>
<p>AssetManager at <a href="https://assetmanager.pxnter.at">https://assetmanager.pxnter.at</a> is operated by Pintér Bence, Vienna, Austria. The operator is the controller responsible for the processing described in this notice. Contact: <a href="mailto:support@pxnter.at">support@pxnter.at</a>.</p>
<p>AssetManager is a free personal technology inventory application. There are no payments or advertisements. Personal data is not sold or used for advertising.</p>
<h2>2. Categories of Personal Data, Purposes and Legal Bases</h2>
<p><strong>Accounts:</strong> name, username, email address, password hash, account identifiers, creation/update times, verification status and authentication/reset information. These support registration, sign-in, account management, email verification and password recovery. Passwords are stored as hashes, not in plaintext. Required registration fields are needed to create an account; public assets can be browsed without one.</p>
<p><strong>Inventory:</strong> device and component names, types, manufacturer, model, model number, serial number, status, condition, acquisition condition and method, purchase date/price/currency, seller, warranty expiry, location, description, specifications, tags, ownership links, visibility, view totals and record timestamps, including trash/deletion markers. Only relevant fields supplied by the user or generated by the application are stored. Many fields are optional; leaving optional information blank does not prevent basic inventory use. The forms identify required fields. Inventory information can also be personal data when linked to an account.</p>
<p><strong>Technical operation:</strong> connections expose an IP address and request information to the server. Session records and technical logs may contain account/session identifiers, browser information, timestamps, request paths, errors and mail-delivery information. They support authentication, security, troubleshooting and delivery. Public asset records store a view total. The total is not a public list of visitors.</p>
<p><strong>Support:</strong> correspondence, sender details and information submitted by the data subject are processed to handle service enquiries, account requests, data-protection requests and reports of abuse. Passwords must not be submitted by email.</p>
<p>Account and inventory processing, requested sharing and service emails rely on Article 6(1)(b) GDPR where necessary to provide the service requested by the user. Security, proportionate technical logging and abuse prevention rely on Article 6(1)(f): the legitimate interest in operating a secure, reliable service. Support is based on Article 6(1)(b) for service requests or Article 6(1)(f) for other enquiries. Specific legal duties may require processing under Article 6(1)(c). Where consent is required for an additional purpose, it must be obtained separately; this notice itself is not consent.</p>
<h2>3. Visibility and Disclosure of Asset Information</h2>
<p>Other visitors cannot access private inventory through the public pages. Setting an asset to public makes its name, manufacturer, model, asset type and all entered specifications available together with the account username. Guests can access public assets through Explore or a shared URL. View totals may be used to rank public assets.</p>
<p>The dedicated model-number, serial-number, status, condition, purchase, seller, warranty, location and description fields are not part of the public display. Email addresses, password hashes and private account details are excluded from this public display.</p>
<p>Specification fields contain user-defined text. Their contents are included in public sharing, including information that would remain private if entered in a separate, non-public field. Users must therefore refrain from entering addresses, credentials, serial numbers or other confidential information in public names or specifications.</p>
<p>Publication may be discontinued by changing the asset visibility to private or deleting the asset. This removes public access through AssetManager but cannot automatically erase screenshots, copies or search-engine caches created by others.</p>
<h2>4. Recipients, Hosting and Electronic Communications</h2>
<p>The operator can access data as necessary to administer the service and resolve requests. Hosting is provided by Rackhost Zrt., registered office: 6722 Szeged, Tisza Lajos körút 41., Hungary; <a href="https://www.rackhost.hu">https://www.rackhost.hu</a>. Rackhost publishes its data-processing terms at <a href="https://www.rackhost.hu/dpa">https://www.rackhost.hu/dpa</a>. Hosting support, infrastructure operation and legally required disclosures may involve the provider or authorised subprocessors.</p>
<p>Service email is sent through the operator's mail server. Delivery necessarily involves the recipient's email provider and may involve processing outside the EEA depending on that provider. Publicly shared information is accessible worldwide. Exclusive processing within the European Union by all recipients and providers is not represented or guaranteed.</p>
<h2>5. Cookies and Authentication</h2>
<p>AssetManager uses session and security cookies for sign-in and protected forms, and a persistent sign-in mechanism where the user selects “Remember me”. Blocking these can prevent account functions from working. AssetManager does not use advertising cookies. Nonessential tracking must not be introduced without the information and consent required by applicable law.</p>
<h2>6. Storage Periods and Erasure</h2>
<p>Account and inventory data is retained while the account remains open and the data is necessary to provide the requested inventory service. An item in Trash remains stored until permanently deleted or the account is deleted; moving it to Trash is not permanent erasure.</p>
<p>Users may permanently delete their account through the profile page upon completing the required confirmation. This deletes the account and associated inventory from the application's active database. Erasure may also be requested at <a href="mailto:support@pxnter.at">support@pxnter.at</a>. Eligible deletion requests are completed within 14 days of receipt. Where entitlement is unclear or a statutory exception applies, the operator will provide information concerning the required clarification or the scope and basis of continued retention; statutory rights and deadlines remain unaffected.</p>
<p>Support correspondence is retained only as needed to resolve the enquiry and necessary follow-up, or a specific legal obligation or dispute. Erasure of such correspondence may be requested separately. Technical logs and session/reset information are retained only as needed for their security, diagnostic and authentication purposes; material needed to investigate a specific incident may be retained for that investigation and any resulting legal claim. These records are separate from inventory deletion.</p>
<p>The operator currently makes no separate application/database backups. Introducing backups will require an updated retention policy and corresponding notice. This statement does not describe any independent infrastructure retention by the hosting provider.</p>
<h2>7. Data Subject Rights and Processing Relating to Minors</h2>
<p>Subject to the applicable statutory conditions, data subjects have rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and data portability, and a right to object to processing based on legitimate interests. Consent may be withdrawn at any time without affecting the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal. Contact <a href="mailto:support@pxnter.at">support@pxnter.at</a>; proportionate identity verification may be necessary. Requests are normally answered within one month, with legally permitted extensions explained. Complaints may be submitted to the Austrian Datenschutzbehörde (<a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at">https://www.dsb.gv.at</a>) or another competent supervisory authority. No decisions with legal or similarly significant effects are made solely by automated processing.</p>
<p>Minors' information receives the same protections. Minor users should refrain from disclosing personal information in public specifications and obtain guidance from a parent or legal guardian. Where parental authorisation is legally required, it must be obtained. The profanity filter is not a guarantee that all public content is suitable for every age.</p>
<h2>8. Amendments to this Notice</h2>
<p>Material changes to processing will be explained through an updated notice and appropriate notification. New processing requiring consent will not be authorised merely by changing this notice.</p>
